course: dictionary
lesson: 14574
title: Pinwheel: one word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and pinwheel is one of them. Context tells you which meaning the writer means. «Maya held the pinwheel up, and it spun round in the breeze.» The breeze and the paper blades show it is a toy.
explain: «On Bonfire Night, the pinwheel fizzed and spun on the fence, throwing out bright sparks.» Fireworks and sparks show this pinwheel is a firework, also called a Catherine wheel.
explain: «Mum rolled up the ham and cheese and cut the pinwheels into slices for lunch.» Cutting slices from a roll tells you the pinwheel is a round spiral shape. Always test your meaning in the sentence to check it fits.
fact: A pinwheel is a noun, so it is a thing.
fact: «Pinwheel» means a toy made of paper or plastic blades on a stick that spins in the wind.
fact: In the UK, a pinwheel toy is called a windmill.
fact: «Pinwheel» can also mean a firework that spins round, also called a Catherine wheel.
fact: «Pinwheel» can mean a round spiral shape, such as pinwheel sandwiches or biscuits.
exercise: «Maya held the pinwheel up, and it spun round in the breeze.» What is a pinwheel here? | A firework that fizzes on the ground | A bird that flies in circles | A round sandwich in a lunchbox | *A toy made of paper blades on a stick
exercise: «On Bonfire Night, the pinwheel fizzed and spun, throwing out bright sparks.» What kind of pinwheel is this? | A cake with cream on top | A sandwich with ham inside | *A firework, also called a Catherine wheel | A toy for the wind
exercise: «Mum cut the pinwheels into slices for lunch.» What shape are the pinwheels? | A flat square | A tall triangle | A long straight line | *A round spiral
test: «The pinwheel on the stick spun faster as the wind blew harder.» In the UK, what is this toy usually called? | *Windmill | Pinwheel sandwich | Catherine wheel | Firework
test: «Ali made a pinwheel from paper and a stick, and it turned in the wind.» Which meaning fits best? | A round biscuit with jam | A spiral of ham and cheese | A firework that sparks | *A toy that spins in the wind
exam: «Ali made a pinwheel from paper and a stick.» What does pinwheel mean here? | A spiral sandwich | A round cake | *A toy that spins in the wind | A firework
